    "body": "minimal repro difference between `console.dir` vs `console.log` + `JSON.stringify`:\n\n```js\n> console.dir(Object.assign(Object.create(null), {'foo':'bar'}))\n[Object: null prototype] { foo: 'bar' }\n> console.log(JSON.stringify(Object.assign(Object.create(null), {'foo':'bar'})))\n{\"foo\":\"bar\"}\n```\n\nReal world use case: `Object.create(null)` is used to construct graphql-js's AST types. The `[Object: null prototype]` adds visual noise when using the REPL to interact with objects -- console.json would be a great convenience.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
